      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Review from Jetski] Since `has_starlark_session()` is true for every target in the build (including builtin C++ targets), calling both `ScheduleBackgroundStarlarkResolution` and `ScheduleBackgroundTargetChecks` posts two separate worker-pool tasks per target and runs `RunStarlarkRule` (which mutates `dependency_output_alias_`) concurrently with `RunChecksAfterResolution` on the same `Target`.\n\nCould `ScheduleBackgroundStarlarkResolution`\u0027s worker lambda run `target-\u003eRunChecksAfterResolution(\u0026err)` right after posting the main-thread completion task? That keeps dependent unblocking off the critical path while halving worker-pool task overhead and avoiding concurrent execution on the same `Target`.\n\n(Also, nit on the comment: `Scheduler::ScheduleWork` synchronously increments `work_count_` and the worker lambda increments it again before `PostTask`, so the relative call order here doesn\u0027t affect `work_count_` staying non-zero.)",
