      "message": "[Review from Jetski] Two issues here:\n1. `target` is unconditionally dereferenced on lines 63-64 (`target-\u003eSetToolchain(...)` and `target-\u003eOnResolved(err)`) after removing the `CHECK`, making the `target \u0026\u0026` check on line 65 too late if a non-target item is ever defined.\n2. More broadly, `Builder::ResolveItem` never calls `Target::OnResolved` on targets (only `TestWithScope` and unit tests do). If `Target::OnResolved(Err* err)` itself calls `RunStarlarkRule(err)` between `OnResolvedWithoutChecks(err)` and `RunChecksAfterResolution(err)` when `has_starlark_session()` is true, `TestWithScope` wouldn\u0027t need to change at all, and direct `target.OnResolved(\u0026err)` calls in other unit tests would also execute Starlark rules.",
